# Docker users: with docker compose up, only the model key matters here - the DSN is set by compose.
# ---- SereneDB (required) ----
# Local Docker setup from the README:
#   docker run -d --name serenedb -p 7890:7890 -e POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me \
#     -v serenedb-data:/var/lib/serenedb serenedb/serenedb:26.09.2
# The password is required: connections from your computer into Docker count as network connections.
# Either format works (in the URL format, percent-encode special characters in the password, e.g. @ -> %40):
SERENEDB_DSN=postgresql://postgres:change-me@localhost:7890/postgres
# SERENEDB_DSN=host=localhost port=7890 dbname=postgres user=postgres password=change-me

# ---- Model provider: only for the web app and the terminal (MCP uses your client's model) ----
# Uncomment ONE provider block below. anthropic is the default.

# anthropic: set exactly ONE of these (the API rejects requests that carry both)
# LOGIQ_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=...          # bearer / OAuth token instead of an API key
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://...    # only if your token is for a gateway or proxy
# LOGIQ_EFFORT=medium               # Claude effort: low | medium | high | xhigh | max

# nvidia: NVIDIA API catalog (build.nvidia.com)
# LOGIQ_PROVIDER=nvidia
# NVIDIA_API_KEY=nvapi-...
# LOGIQ_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b   # must support tool calling; see README for alternatives

# openai: any OpenAI-compatible server, e.g. Ollama
# LOGIQ_PROVIDER=openai
# LOGIQ_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LOGIQ_MODEL=qwen3:14b
# LOGIQ_API_KEY=...                  # only if the server needs one

# LOGIQ_MODEL overrides the default model for any provider (anthropic default: claude-opus-5-5)
